{"run_id": "planned-4207-s01-e9fc56", "t": 12.51, "type": "model_call", "step": 5, "purpose": "execute", "model": "gpt-4.1-mini-2025-04-14", "stop_reason": "tool_use", "latency_s": 1.703, "usage": {"input_tokens": 3365, "output_tokens": 206, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "prompt_tokens": 3365}, "cost_usd": 0.0016756, "tool_calls": [{"name": "issues_comment", "input": {"issue": "issue-4207", "body": "label: bug\nfile: src/export/scheduler.ts\n\nThe issue involves a bug where the first scheduled export does not send on the day it is created, specifically for weekly schedules created early in the morning. The relevant code in src/export/scheduler.ts shows that the next scheduled run for weekly cadence is always set to 7 days after the current run time (nextRunAt sets the next run exactly one week later, regardless of the creation time). This means a schedule created just before or around the intended run hour will effectively skip the first run because the code advances the run date by a full week instead of checking if the current day/time should still trigger an export. This explains why the first weekly export doesn't send on the day the schedule is created but instead one week later. Further investigation and a fix might require adjusting the nextRunAt logic to handle the first run correctly based on creation time and run hour."}}], "tools": ["issues_comment"], "request": null, "text": ""}
